    "teacher_markdown": "## Level 3 — Teaching Tips (HTML / Structure)\r\n\r\n- **Reinforce structure vs. style.**  \r\n  This level focuses only on *structure* (what appears on the page), not colors or fonts yet.\r\n\r\n- **Watch for under-specific prompts.**  \r\n  If students write something vague like “make me a gardening app,” push them to include:\r\n  - What information appears  \r\n  - What buttons exist  \r\n  - How missing data should be handled  \r\n\r\n- **Ensure they request only `index.html`.**  \r\n  AI may generate CSS or extra files unless students clearly state:  \r\n  > “Generate only the `index.html` file.”\r\n\r\n- **Address the “AI must be right” misconception.**  \r\n  Encourage students to skim the output and ask:\r\n  - Is anything missing?  \r\n  - Are edge cases handled?  \r\n  - Does this match the plan from Level 1?\r\n\r\n- **Connect back to planning.**  \r\n  Remind students they already defined requirements, constraints, and edge cases — now they are translating that thinking into HTML.\r\n\r\n\r\n"
  },
